# Base packages with no aarch64 build under the name Omarchy names them, in any
# repository Omarchy configures (verified against the live [omarchy], Arch
# Linux ARM [core] [extra] [alarm] and [aur] databases; see
# docs/pi/package-compatibility.md). omarchy-pkg-defaults leaves them out of
# every aarch64 platform's set; their replacements join
# omarchy-aarch64.packages. Delete an entry the day its name resolves upstream,
# and its replacement with it.
nvim
# Arch renamed the package; Arch Linux ARM still ships neovim without
# provides=nvim, so the manifest name fails to resolve there. Replacement:
# neovim (omarchy-aarch64.packages).
vi
# No vi package exists in any configured aarch64 repository, and no Omarchy
# code invokes /usr/bin/vi. Replacement: vim (omarchy-aarch64.packages).
